      "content": "That's a great level of detail, thanks. One thing my students always struggle with is the 'suddenness' of it—how it feels like the reaction just hits them out of nowhere once the knife breaks the cells. Is there a specific reason for that rapid onset, or is it just the volatility of the propanethial-S-oxide?",
